{
  "info": {
    "name": "Image Processing Service",
    "description": "Collection Postman du projet. Lancer d'abord POST /register puis POST /login : le jeton est enregistré automatiquement dans la variable `token`.",
    "schema": "https://schema.getpostman.com/json/collection/v2.1.0/collection.json"
  },
  "variable": [
    {
      "key": "baseUrl",
      "value": "http://localhost:3001"
    },
    {
      "key": "email",
      "value": "salut@example.com"
    },
    {
      "key": "password",
      "value": "motdepasse123"
    },
    {
      "key": "token",
      "value": ""
    },
    {
      "key": "imageId",
      "value": ""
    },
    {
      "key": "derivedId",
      "value": ""
    }
  ],
  "item": [
    {
      "name": "Health",
      "request": {
        "method": "GET",
        "url": "{{baseUrl}}/health",
        "description": "200 si l'API et la base répondent, 503 sinon."
      }
    },
    {
      "name": "Register",
      "request": {
        "method": "POST",
        "header": [
          {
            "key": "Content-Type",
            "value": "application/json"
          }
        ],
        "url": "{{baseUrl}}/register",
        "body": {
          "mode": "raw",
          "raw": "{\n  \"email\": \"{{email}}\",\n  \"password\": \"{{password}}\"\n}"
        },
        "description": "201 { id, email } | 400 validation ou JSON malformé | 409 e-mail déjà pris."
      }
    },
    {
      "name": "Login",
      "event": [
        {
          "listen": "test",
          "script": {
            "type": "text/javascript",
            "exec": [
              "if (pm.response.code === 200) {",
              "  pm.collectionVariables.set('token', pm.response.json().token);",
              "}"
            ]
          }
        }
      ],
      "request": {
        "method": "POST",
        "header": [
          {
            "key": "Content-Type",
            "value": "application/json"
          }
        ],
        "url": "{{baseUrl}}/login",
        "body": {
          "mode": "raw",
          "raw": "{\n  \"email\": \"{{email}}\",\n  \"password\": \"{{password}}\"\n}"
        },
        "description": "200 { token } (stocké dans la variable `token`) | 400 validation | 401 identifiants incorrects."
      }
    },
    {
      "name": "Upload image",
      "request": {
        "method": "POST",
        "header": [],
        "auth": {
          "type": "bearer",
          "bearer": [
            {
              "key": "token",
              "value": "{{token}}",
              "type": "string"
            }
          ]
        },
        "url": "{{baseUrl}}/images",
        "body": {
          "mode": "formdata",
          "formdata": [
            {
              "key": "image",
              "type": "file",
              "src": []
            }
          ]
        },
        "description": "Choisir un fichier JPEG, PNG ou WebP dans le champ `image` (10 Mo et 8000 px par côté maximum). Le type est vérifié par le contenu, pas par l'extension. 201 métadonnées | 400 fichier manquant/illisible | 401 | 413 trop lourd ou trop grand | 415 format non supporté. L'id de l'image créée est enregistré dans la variable `imageId`."
      },
      "event": [
        {
          "listen": "test",
          "script": {
            "type": "text/javascript",
            "exec": [
              "if (pm.response.code === 201) {",
              "  pm.collectionVariables.set('imageId', pm.response.json().id);",
              "}"
            ]
          }
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "name": "Get image",
      "request": {
        "method": "GET",
        "header": [],
        "auth": {
          "type": "bearer",
          "bearer": [
            {
              "key": "token",
              "value": "{{token}}",
              "type": "string"
            }
          ]
        },
        "url": "{{baseUrl}}/images/{{imageId}}",
        "description": "Renvoie le fichier (flux) avec son Content-Type. 200 | 401 | 404 (image inconnue OU appartenant à un autre utilisateur : jamais 403)."
      }
    },
    {
      "name": "List images",
      "request": {
        "method": "GET",
        "header": [],
        "auth": {
          "type": "bearer",
          "bearer": [
            {
              "key": "token",
              "value": "{{token}}",
              "type": "string"
            }
          ]
        },
        "url": {
          "raw": "{{baseUrl}}/images?page=1&limit=10",
          "host": [
            "{{baseUrl}}"
          ],
          "path": [
            "images"
          ],
          "query": [
            {
              "key": "page",
              "value": "1"
            },
            {
              "key": "limit",
              "value": "10"
            }
          ]
        },
        "description": "Liste paginée de TES images, la plus récente d'abord. Défauts : page=1, limit=10 ; limit max 50. 200 { items, page, limit, total } | 400 paramètres hors bornes | 401."
      }
    },
    {
      "name": "Transform image",
      "event": [
        {
          "listen": "test",
          "script": {
            "type": "text/javascript",
            "exec": [
              "if (pm.response.code === 201) {",
              "  pm.collectionVariables.set('derivedId', pm.response.json().id);",
              "}"
            ]
          }
        }
      ],
      "request": {
        "method": "POST",
        "header": [
          {
            "key": "Content-Type",
            "value": "application/json"
          }
        ],
        "auth": {
          "type": "bearer",
          "bearer": [
            {
              "key": "token",
              "value": "{{token}}",
              "type": "string"
            }
          ]
        },
        "url": "{{baseUrl}}/images/{{imageId}}/transform",
        "body": {
          "mode": "raw",
          "raw": "{\n  \"crop\": { \"x\": 0, \"y\": 0, \"width\": 200, \"height\": 200 },\n  \"rotate\": 90,\n  \"flip\": false,\n  \"mirror\": true,\n  \"resize\": { \"width\": 300, \"fit\": \"inside\" },\n  \"filter\": \"sepia\",\n  \"format\": \"webp\",\n  \"quality\": 80\n}"
        },
        "description": "Crée une image DÉRIVÉE (l'original n'est jamais modifié). Toutes les clés sont optionnelles, au moins une opération est requise. Ordre d'application : orientation EXIF → crop → rotate → flip → mirror → resize → filter → format/quality. rotate : entier de -360 à 360 (sens horaire). flip = vertical, mirror = horizontal. resize : width et/ou height (1 à 8000), fit = cover|contain|fill|inside|outside (défaut inside). filter = grayscale|sepia. format = jpeg|png|webp. quality 1-100 (jpeg/webp seulement). 201 { id, originalId, format, sizeBytes, width, height, createdAt } (l'id est enregistré dans `derivedId`) | 400 paramètres invalides | 401 | 404 image inconnue ou d'un autre utilisateur. Pour voir le résultat : adapter l'URL de « Get image » avec {{derivedId}}."
      }
    }
  ]
}
